WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:04.370
Ever read that book 1001 Movies to Watch Before
You Die?

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:06.360
Well, this is… not that.

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:11.940
The following action titles all share a dubious
distinction: They each currently hold a zero

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:14.030
percent rating on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:17.860
Let's take a look at some of the genre's biggest-ever
bombs… before they blow!

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:20.640
Ecks vs Sever: Yikes

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:27.580
This is probably what happens if you ask actress
Lucy Liu about the disastrous 2002 film Ballistic:

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:28.200
Ecks vs. Sever.

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:41.960
If you've ever heard of this stinker, it's
probably because an astonishing 116 critics

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:42.440
have branded it "rotten."

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:45.870
In fact, it currently holds the record for
the most negative Rotten Tomatoes reviews

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:48.389
of all time… and it's easy to see why.

00:00:48.389 --> 00:00:51.979
Lucy Liu plays Sever, a vengeful ex-DIA agent.

00:00:51.979 --> 00:00:57.420
Antonio Banderas portrays Jeremiah Ecks, a
former FBI tracker with amazing facial hair.

00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:01.749
Together, they wear form-fitting black outfits,
blow things up, and perform martial arts.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:02.500
That's pretty much it.

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:13.560
We'll leave you with the film's best line
of dialogue:

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:24.780
Derailed is a disaster

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:29.000
"We're taking the 681 to Munich."

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:30.560
"Let's get a few things straight Jack.

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:32.360
I don't need you, nor do I want you."

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:34.760
It's time to talk about Derailed.

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:38.600
Not the 2005 film Derailed starring Jennifer
Aniston and Clive Owen.

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:40.520
Nor the Korean Derailed from 2016.

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:43.020
Nor the Canadian Derailed from 2017.

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:45.340
We're talking about the real Derailed.

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:47.460
The Jean-Claude Van Damme Derailed.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:53.510
This spine-tingling 2002 opus features trains,
Van Damme kicking people, and Van Damme kicking

00:01:53.510 --> 00:01:55.039
people on trains.

00:01:55.039 --> 00:01:59.229
If disposable action movies had a face, it
would undoubtedly be Van Damme's.

00:01:59.229 --> 00:02:04.289
The actor has a startling 20-year streak of
rotten films that started in 1988 and wasn't

00:02:04.289 --> 00:02:09.620
broken until he poked fun at his own public
image with the meta-action satire JCVD in

00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:10.120
2008.

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:22.480
Derailed is probably the cake topper here,
but it's worth noting that the 1999 adventure

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:27.600
Desert Heat and the 2001 head-scratcher The
Order also have zero percent scores.

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:37.640
What a shame

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:41.860
There was a time when the public trusted the
comedic stylings of the Wayans family.

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:46.700
In Living Color was fantastic… and we hadn't
been burned by White Chicks or Little Man

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:47.200
yet.

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:49.380
"Goo goo, gaa gaa?"

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:55.090
Released in 1994, Keenan Ivory Wayans' A Low
Down Dirty Shame was the sketch star's attempt

00:02:55.090 --> 00:02:58.240
at an action comedy which he wrote, starred
in, and directed.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:01.570
The title alone invited plenty of criticals
jabs.

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:06.040
And the contrived writing and clichéd fight
scenes resulted in universal critical failure.

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:08.180
Oh, and can we talk about the offensive gay
stereotypes?

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:09.660
"The Bernard?"

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:10.680
"Yes!

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:11.180
It's me."

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:13.060
"Homewrecker!

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:13.680
He's with me!"

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:15.900
"What?"

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:16.800
"I can't believe you just did that!"

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:19.240
Dark Tide is deadly

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:24.620
As a general rule of thumb, sharks just don't
work on-screen unless there's a tornado, or

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:29.080
an astronaut is using it as a re-entry device.

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:40.920
But apparently the filmmakers behind the 2012
snooze-fest Dark Tide didn't get that memo.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:45.750
Halle Berry stars as Kate, a professional
"shark whisperer" who clearly has a lot of

00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:46.240
integrity:

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:48.060
"'Cuz I'm the shark whisperer…

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:49.280
Legend of the deep!

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:50.820
… Stop it, stop it!"

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:51.320
"Stop what?!"

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:53.600
"Stop using me to make money!"

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:56.480
Someone was clearly angling for another Oscar.

00:03:56.880 --> 00:04:00.600
Anyway, Kate is intimidatingly knowledgeable
about all things shark.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:01.620
"She's beautiful!"

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:02.220
"She's a he."

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:03.700
"How do you know it's a male?"

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:06.500
"Cuz I can see claspers on his anal fins."

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:10.200
In fact, you can tell she's definitely a shark
expert.

00:04:10.780 --> 00:04:17.940
"So sharks have really sensitive snouts, so
they can actually feel your heart rate, so

00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:19.280
they sense nervousness."

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:23.260
Running low on funds, Kate agrees to take
a wealthy family on a shark tour through a

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:25.590
dangerous part of the sea called Shark Alley.

00:04:25.590 --> 00:04:27.320
You probably know where this is going.

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:30.540
Dark Tide pulled in less than half a million
dollars at the box office.

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:34.810
That isn't too shocking, considering you've
already seen the best part of the movie.

00:04:34.810 --> 00:04:36.200
"'Cuz I'm the shark whisperer…

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:36.980
Legend of the deep!

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:38.800
… Stop it, stop it!"

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:39.540
"Stop what?!"

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:41.980
"Stop using me to make money!"

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:44.680
Precious Cargo: Abort mission

00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:49.720
Released in 2016, Precious Cargo is a film
that's got it all: Bruce Willis...

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:51.960
Actually, it's just got Bruce Willis.

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:53.180
"Damn straight."

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:57.320
Willis plays the same character he always
plays: A dyed-in-wool Bruce Willis type.

00:04:57.500 --> 00:04:59.440
"I don't make deals with people who steal
from me.

00:05:00.580 --> 00:05:01.560
It's not good for business."

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:05.460
The beyond generic thriller was universally
panned by critics.

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:09.120
One reviewer aptly called the film "just another
VOD craptacular."

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:14.780
"I had him."

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:20.360
You're probably wondering if there's anything
we can recommend about Precious Cargo.

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:21.740
"Nope."

